+# Image generation prompts
+
+Generated with the built-in image generation tool. Each image was generated independently from text without reference images, then saved as a 1024×1024 PNG using sips.
+
+## styles/357-little-nemo.png
+
+Create one square 1024x1024 image, freshly generated entirely from this text with no reference images. Use case: illustration-story.
+Style is the absolute priority: Winsor McCay's Little Nemo in Slumberland, an authentic early-1900s Sunday newspaper fantasy illustration. Meticulous elastic pen contours, architectural perspective, flattened lithographic newspaper colors, pale cyan, coral pink, buttery yellow and mint, slight aged-paper printing texture. Art Nouveau whiplash ornament and astonishing dream logic. Make this an original single illustrated scene, not a comic page with lettering.
+A vast fantastical city of elaborate spires, curving staircases and palatial arcades rises among GIANT mushrooms. A fanciful bed has four impossibly long jointed walking legs and strides above the mushroom forest. A woman in her early 30s sits sideways on the mattress enjoying a small cup of coffee, a croissant clearly visible on a breakfast tray beside her. She has curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater. Draw her with McCay-like simplified cartoon anatomy and expressive gestures, not naturalistic portrait anatomy.
+Wide, expansive, sweeping dreamscape viewed from a high oblique angle, bed and woman amid gigantic fantastical architecture. Her full body is visible but the extraordinary setting dominates; make her face large enough to resolve glasses and freckles. Exaggerated scale and fanciful perspective; beautiful precise hand-drawn linework and flat period color printing must determine every shape. No photography, no photographic shading, no 3D, no modern cinematic rendering. No text, lettering, speech balloons, captions, titles, signatures, logos or watermarks anywhere.
+
+## styles/358-beatrix-potter.png
+
+Create one square 1024x1024 image, freshly generated entirely from this text with no reference images. Use case: illustration-story.
+An authentic Beatrix Potter-style delicate watercolor and very fine ink storybook vignette on generous unpainted warm ivory paper. Soft muted moss and sage greens, earth browns, transparent washes, restrained rosy cheeks, botanical and natural-history precision. Small-scale intimate English countryside charm; delicate fur and tiny wild plants observed with a naturalist's care. The painting softly dissolves into blank paper around the edges.
+A woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater kneels comfortably in the grass at a tiny country tea gathering. She enjoys her own coffee from a small china cup, while two rabbits in little jackets share tea with her. A croissant lies nearby on a small saucer on their low picnic tea spread. Give her gently simplified Edwardian storybook anatomy and a modest, relaxed three-quarter pose. The rabbits are accurately rabbit-shaped beneath their miniature tailored jackets. A hedgerow, a little mossy stone wall and English meadow flowers suggest the countryside.
+Intimate mid-distance eye-level grouping, figures clustered low within the square with abundant airy ivory space above and around them. Soft diffuse daylight expressed with translucent watercolor rather than digital light effects. Hand-painted watercolor pooling and feathery dry-brush textures, spare fine ink accents, no hard decorative frame. Let the authentic illustration style fully determine the proportions, pose, setting and medium. No photography, no photographic filter, no 3D or glossy digital fantasy. No text, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks.
+
+## styles/359-rackham.png
+
+Create one square 1024x1024 image, freshly generated entirely from this text with no reference images. Use case: illustration-story.
+Arthur Rackham fairy-tale illustration: astonishingly fine nervous pen lines, tangled calligraphic roots and branches, crooked silhouettes, fine hatching, translucent sepia-muted watercolor on old ivory paper. Muted umber, smoky olive, tobacco, parchment and desaturated auburn with a subdued mustard accent. Eerie woodland enchantment; hand-inked and watercolor painted throughout.
+Close, asymmetrical profile view of a woman in her early 30s, seated among twisted roots, her upper body and face prominent in the lower foreground. She has curly auburn shoulder-length hair rendered as intricate ink tendrils, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater. She raises a coffee cup toward her lips with quiet enjoyment, with a croissant plainly nearby on a broad root. Her figure has the angular, delicately drawn anatomy and wistful long-nosed profile of a golden-age fairy-tale illustration.
+A huge gnarled anthropomorphic tree bends its ancient face toward her, filling the upper image with a knotted trunk and long fingerlike branches. Small mischievous goblins peer from root crevices and a few delicate winged faeries circle the fragrant coffee steam. The densely interwoven tree and roots form a skewed natural enclosure. Close foreground against receding murky woods, off-center composition, curious rather than horrific. Every shadow is ink hatching or a thin brown-green watercolor wash. Style dictates the anatomy and space; no photorealistic skin, no photographic lighting, no lens effects, no 3D, no modern digital concept-art finish. No text, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks.
+
+## styles/360-kay-nielsen.png
